    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Following the 1925 Eulchuk flood, Japanese authorities built a drainage pumping station in 1926 at what is now Magok‑dong.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Yangcheon_District",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "That pumping station is the only surviving colonial‑era agricultural drainage pump in Korea, protecting farmland from flooding.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Yangcheon_District",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The pump station’s operation enabled double‑cropping of rice, feeding Japanese markets during the colonial period.",
